When a character dies while having {{i|Judas' Shadow}} in their inventory, they will respawn as '''Black Judas''' (also known as '''Dark Judas'''). Black Judas spawns with two {{E|Black Heart}}s, a damage multiplier of 2x, and a base speed of 1.1. Black Judas has the highest damage multiplier of all the playable characters.

{{dlc|nr}} Black Judas can still gain Red Heart containers despite starting with none.<br>
{{dlc|r}} Black Judas cannot gain Red Heart containers; items that grant Red Heart containers (including empty ones) will give him the same amount of {{E|Black Heart}}s instead.

Black Judas is considered by the game to be a separate character from Judas, but Black Judas 
counts as Judas for the achievements and unlocks that require Judas, including his [[Completion Mark]]s. {{dlc+|r}} He will also receive {{c|Tainted Judas|r}}' bonus effects when using {{i|Dark Arts}}.{{dlc-}}

== Notes ==
* The {{i|The Book of Belial|text=Book of Belial}}'s damage increase is very powerful; it should be kept, if possible, until the player has enough damage from other sources.
** {{dlc|na}} The Book of Belial also guarantees a {{R|Devil Room}} or {{R|Angel Room}} to open after defeating a boss while holding it.
** {{dlc|a}} The Book of Belial increases the chance by 12.5% instead of guaranteeing one.
* Due to Judas' low starting health, health upgrades should be prioritized. {{R|Devil Room}} deals can also be risky, if not unaffordable.
** {{i|Dead Cat}} has effectively no downside if found early, as Judas already has one Red Heart container. It is also one of the {{tf|Guppy}} items.
** Items that activate on low health, such as the {{i|Scapular}}, {{t|Monkey Paw}}, {{I|Glyph of Balance}}, and {{i|Whore of Babylon}}, can be triggered very easily.

== Item Interactions ==
* {{i|Birthright}}: {{I|The Book of Belial}} becomes a passive item that can be held beneath other active items, similar to {{I|Book of Virtues}}. The Book of Belial's damage boost scales with the amount of charges the active item above it has.
** The damage boost may not work with single-use items, unlimited use items, timed recharges, or items that do not follow normal room charge rules ({{I|Isaac's Tears}}, etc). It also has special interactions with certain items — see [[The Book of Belial#Synergies|The Book of Belial]] for more information.
** Stacks with Book of Virtues.
** If Judas is not currently holding The Book of Belial, he receives it.
* {{i|Blood of the Martyr}}: Synergizes with The Book of Belial for an extra 1.5x damage multiplier.

